    },
    {
      "id": "slice6-s7-quantile-coincidence",
      "file": "paper/source/chapters/13_s04b_joint_quantiles.tex",
      "locator": "caption of Table tab:s04b-joint-quantiles",
      "finding": "The S7 immigrant-only and total rows share Q25, Min and Max. The caption now gives the algebraic reason and the correct intersection: S7 has 19/20 immigrant fits and 9/20 total fits at n=0, but the two intensities coincide only on the 9/20 seeds where both select n=0. One-sided zero selections do not make the intensities identical. Those nine seeds supply the shared minimum, maximum and both lower-quartile order statistics; the upper quartile uses a seed with total n=0.98 and immigrant n=0.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "id": "slice6-line75-score-attribution",
      "file": "paper/source/chapters/13_continuous_local_inhibition.tex",
      "locator": "line 75, Section 13.4.1",
      "finding": "The 75,313.9 versus 59,415.5 and -15,898.4 figures were presented as the training score slope of the unit-mark immigrant-only LI law. They are the score slope of the separate total-intensity EP+ attenuation model lambda=lambda_0 exp(-eta G) in Section 11.5. The repaired paragraph gives the immigrant-only LI derivative, which weights each event by B(t_i,z_i)/lambda_0(t_i,z_i) and integrates against B(t,z), and explicitly attributes the three EP+ literals to Section sec:california-eta-profiles.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "id": "slice6-raw-math-tokens",
      "file": "paper/source/chapters/13_continuous_local_inhibition.tex",
      "locator": "lines 30, 61, 73, 90, 107-109, 113, 120-128, 144, 153, 155, 159, 173-178, 205, 211, 251, 255",
      "finding": "Raw ASCII variables, unformatted assignments, raw scientific notation and the legacy 'in IV' reference were normalized to math mode and an internal chapter cross-reference. Every pre-edit numeric value is retained; the only added values are the signed +0.0002 tolerance endpoint and the S7 explanatory counts.",
